Hi, everybody.

Just wanted to let you know about some Linux classes being offered 
in NYC.

There are being run by a group called New York Linux Scene (NYLXS)
We are running these classes to empower New Yorkers through the use
of technology and Free Software.

The Classes are 

Linux 1  -  Unix 1  -  Perl 1  -  Perl 2.

More classes to come, there are 8 in our curriculum right now.

So, if you are in the area, and are interested, come check us out!

Incidentally, we are involved with a lot more as well.  Such as 
bringing Linux to schools, getting involved witth wiring Brooklyn 
Borrough Hall, and even lobying our elected representatives, 
educating them on the issues that are important to our community.

Flyers for these classes available at:

http://sangretoro.net/documents/


If you can't make these, check up with us or send me an email and I'll
let you know when we run our next class.  We run them about every 5 weeks.


- Paul Rodriguez
paulr@nylxs.com




Linux 1 - 

Wednesdays from 7:00-10:30PM
Rosensweig and Maffia
845 3rd Avenue
13th Floor

March 30, April 10, 17, 24, May 1

This 5 week course introduces Free Software and the
Linux operating system. Through lectures and hands on
text and graphical installations, students will
develop an understanding of how Linux works and is
structured. The class begins with an overview of how
information is stored and accessed on the computer. We
will discuss the concepts of file systems, partitions,
files and their permissions, the Linux directory tree,
and an introduction to the kernel. Students will
perform complete text and graphical installs, as well
as basic network and system configuration.

       * File Systems
       * Partitions
       * Files and Permissions
       * Directory Tree
       * Network Config
       * Modules
       * Intro to Kernel

Unix 1 - 

Mondays 7:00-10:00PM
1600 17th St.
Brooklyn, NY


March 18
March 25
April 8
April 15
April 22

Our Introduction to Unix 1 class introduces the power
of the Command Line Interface (CLI) and some of the
basic tools Unix makes available.  Built into every
Unix system, the CLI is the strongest and most
essential tool to unlock the power of all Unix
systems.  This class will demystify the CLI, and help
explain when and how to use it to make the most use of
your computing experience.  Going beyond simple
commands, the class introduces Shell scripting, Vi,
the GCC compiler, network and system administration.

       * Review of Unix Tools
       * Introduction to the CLI
       * Basic Commands
       * Intro to Shell Programming
       * Vi and Programming Editors
       * Advanced Shell Commands
       * GCC Compiler
       * RPM Tools
       * Networking Tools




Perl 1 - 

Thrusday 6:30-10:30PM
Thaumaturgix
19 West 44th Street
18th Floor

March 21
April 11
April 18
April 25
May 5

Our Introduction to Perl Programming class provides
you with the training you need to understand and work
productively with Perl.  Special emphasis is given to
proper, real-world program-ming techniques.  This
class will take you through understanding Perls
underlying structure, writing your own programs, and
learning to to tackle and manage real world
programming problems.

       * Operators
       * Variables
       * Functions
       * Control Structures
       * Regular Expressions
       * Pattern Matching
       * Scope
       * Use of Subroutines
       * Object Oriented Programming


Perl 2 - 

Tuesdays 5:30-9:30PM
ICG
254 West 31st St. 
(and 8th Ave.)
10th Floor

March 26
April 9
April 16
April 23
April 30

Our Perl 2: Advanced Web Programming with Perl class
builds on the skills developed in Perl 1 to take your
programming to the next level.  Beginning with object
oriented programming, this class will teach you how to
utilize the power of Perl to facillitate effective web
design.  Make the most of your time learning rapid
development and design templating skills.  Learn how
to build and work with database web applications, SQL,
and MySQL.

       * Object Orientation
       * Basic CGI Programming
       * Database Usage and SQL
       * Building Database Web
          Aplications with DBI
       * Basic SQL and MySQL
        Administration
       * Rapid Development     and 
        Web Design Templating
       * Intro to modperl
       * Writing basic Apache modules

